  "details": "**EDIT:** A friend of mine drew my attention to the changelog, which indicates that *\"this currently overrides the main menu setting instead of changing it every time\"*.\n\nI am, however, still confused by this feature's behaviour for these reasons:\n\n1. To enable avatar cloning again, you would need to uncheck the main menu setting before re-checking it again.\n2. Turning off the new 'Auto Disable Cloning' setting in the quick menu doesn't re-enable avatar cloning immediately. You still have to change worlds again. \n\nIs there another way to enable avatar cloning that I'm not aware of? Unchecking and re-checking a box seems like an inelegant UI interaction for situations when you want to briefly enable cloning for someone.\n\n**INITIAL POST:** The 'Auto Disable Cloning' feature seems to work as intended but the UI in the main settings menu doesn't update to show that it worked.\n\n1. Enable avatar cloning by checking the 'Allow Avatar Cloning' option in the main settings menu.\n2. Enable 'Auto Disable Cloning' in the Settings tab of the quick menu.\n3. Go to another world.\n4. Look in the main settings menu and notice that 'Allow Avatar Cloning' is still checked. \n5. Query the API using VRCX, for example, and notice that your avatar cloning was successfully disabled despite the UI not updating.",
